      "id": 1,
      "text": "Arcadia University began as Beaver Female Seminary in 1853, founded by the Methodist Episcopal Church to give young women a liberal arts education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arcadia.edu/about-arcadia/our-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1872 the seminary gained collegiate status and became Beaver College and Musical Institute, expanding beyond women's arts to a full liberal arts college.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arcadia_University",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Grey Towers Castle, built in 1898, now serves as Arcadia University’s main administration building and is a National Historic Landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcadia_University%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Arcadia ranks first in the United States for undergraduate study abroad participation, according to the 2025 Open Doors Report.",
